    images were available to be purchased as prints. The site was well designed
    and the search features were good, but there was no community on the site.
    The niche Corbis pursued was outright ownership of archives and scanning
    on demand. Corbis had recently acquired the Louvre archive, for a reported
    purchase price of over $30 million.
