The quest for long life has spurred the imagination of people in virtually every
era in human history. Ancient Greeks imagined immortal gods, the sixteenth cen-
tury Spanish adventurer Ponce de Leon searched for the fountain of youth, and
21st century scientists tested rodents for life-extending biological compounds.
Until the 1990s, the only proven means of increasing lifespan in any animal was
to reduce its calorie intake; however, for decades scientists did not understand

